  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果や法令ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A fictional municipal council proposes changing the opening hours of a public library to reduce operating expenses.",
          "ja": "架空の自治体議会は運営費削減のため公共図書館の開館時間変更を提案する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Before making a final decision, it organizes a public hearing on a weekday afternoon.",
          "ja": "最終決定前に平日午後の公聴会を開催する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Most speakers support the proposed change, and the council initially regards the meeting as evidence of broad public approval.",
          "ja": "発言者の大半は賛成し議会は当初その会を広い市民支持の証拠と見なす。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A librarian nevertheless questions whether the participants represent the people most affected by the reduction in evening services.",
          "ja": "しかし司書は参加者が夜間サービス縮小の影響を最も受ける人々を代表するのか疑問を持つ。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Many people who visit the library after work or school may be unable to attend a meeting scheduled during the afternoon.",
          "ja": "仕事や学校の後に来館する人の多くは午後の会に参加できないかもしれない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Their absence does not necessarily indicate satisfaction with the proposed arrangement.",
          "ja": "欠席は提案への満足を必ずしも示さない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The council recognizes that the procedure used to collect opinions may influence which opinions become visible to decision makers.",
          "ja": "意見収集手順がどの意見が意思決定者に見えるかに影響し得ると認識する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It therefore examines how the timing and format of consultation could unintentionally exclude certain groups.",
          "ja": "そこで協議の時刻と形式が意図せず特定集団を排除し得る仕組みを検討する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Officials arrange another opportunity for residents to contribute written responses and attend a later meeting.",
          "ja": "文書での回答と後の会への参加機会を整える。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They provide a concise description of the proposal, including the financial constraints that prompted it.",
          "ja": "提案のきっかけとなった財務制約を含む簡潔な説明を提供する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Participants are encouraged to describe alternatives rather than simply express support or opposition.",
          "ja": "賛否だけでなく代替案を述べるよう促す。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The council records the relevant concerns without claiming that the additional responses constitute a statistically representative survey.",
          "ja": "追加回答が統計的な代表調査を構成すると主張せず関連する懸念を記録する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Several alternatives involve reducing services at times when demand is relatively low while retaining some evening access.",
          "ja": "比較的需要の低い時間のサービスを減らし一部の夜間利用を残す案が出る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The council investigates their feasibility and acknowledges that the budget may still require difficult compromises.",
          "ja": "実現可能性を検討し予算上難しい妥協が必要かもしれないと認める。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It explains how the available evidence informed its final decision and identifies concerns that could not be fully addressed.",
          "ja": "どのように根拠が最終決定に影響したか、十分対応できなかった懸念も説明する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The process does not guarantee that every resident will agree with the eventual outcome.",
          "ja": "全住民が結果に賛成する保証はない。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Public consultation is valuable when it reveals relevant information that officials might otherwise overlook.",
          "ja": "協議は職員が見落とすかもしれない関連情報を明らかにするとき価値がある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A meeting with no visible disagreement may provide limited evidence if the people most likely to object cannot participate.",
          "ja": "反対しやすい人が参加できなければ目に見える反対のない会は限られた証拠しか提供しない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A defensible procedure considers barriers to participation without treating every response as an equally representative measure of public opinion.",
          "ja": "正当化可能な手順はすべての回答を世論の同等な代表指標と扱わず参加障壁を考慮する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The purpose of consultation is to improve the basis for public judgment, not merely to produce an appearance of agreement.",
          "ja": "協議の目的は合意の外観を作るだけでなく公共の判断根拠を改善することだ。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
